s1 every setting	:: COREPROTECT_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: Cleared N previews.
s1 every setting	:: Colour of a gate's own name, on both its name sign and its dial sign. One of the sixteen chat colours, such as AQUA, GOLD or LIGHT_PURPLE.
s1 every setting	:: Colour of the destination currently selected on a dial sign. Keep it distinct from the neighbours either side.
s1 every setting	:: Colour of the destinations either side of the selected one on a dial sign.
s1 every setting	:: Colour of the network line on a gate's name sign.
s1 every setting	:: Colour of the owner line on a gate's name sign.
s1 every setting	:: DYNMAP_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: ECONOMY_BUILD_COST = N
s1 every setting	:: ECONOMY_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: ECONOMY_USE_COST = N
s1 every setting	:: Enable Cooldown timers on stargate usage. Timer only activates on passage through wormholes.
s1 every setting	:: Enable Vault economy integration. Requires Vault and an economy plugin. When false every cost below is ignored.
s1 every setting	:: Furthest apart the two ends of a ring pair may be on the ground, in blocks. N is sixteen chunks; gates are the long-haul option. N for no limit.
s1 every setting	:: GATE_DIAL_SPIN = NONE
s1 every setting	:: GATE_IRIS_ANIMATION = sweep
s1 every setting	:: GATE_MATERIAL_GROUPS_AUTODISCOVER
s1 every setting	:: GATE_MATERIAL_GROUPS_AUTODISCOVER = true
s1 every setting	:: GATE_PREVIEW_MAX_BLOCKS = ID
s1 every setting	:: GATE_PREVIEW_MINUTES = N
s1 every setting	:: GATE_RIPPLE = false
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUNDS_ENABLED = true
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_ACTIVATE = block.conduit.activate
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_AMBIENT = ambient.underwater.loop
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_CHEVRON = block.iron_trapdoor.close
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_CLOSE = block.conduit.deactivate
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_IRIS_CLOSE = block.iron_door.close
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_IRIS_OPEN = block.iron_door.open
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_KAWOOSH = entity.player.splash.high_speed
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_LOCK = block.beacon.power_select
s1 every setting	:: GATE_SOUND_VOLUME = N
s1 every setting	:: GATE_VIEW = horizon
s1 every setting	:: GATE_VIEW_FUNNEL = true
s1 every setting	:: GATE_VIEW_FUNNEL_LENGTH = N
s1 every setting	:: GATE_VIEW_FUNNEL_MIN_LENGTH = N
s1 every setting	:: How a dialling gate's inner ring light moves before each chevron locks: TOP, CHEVRON, LAP, FILL, PEGASUS, CHASE, UNIVERSE, OVERSHOOT or NONE. Each is described in the gate guide. TOP rests half a second on the top chevron after each lock, and UNIVERSE turns at its own pace, so both dial a little slower.
s1 every setting	:: How a ring stack deploys: CONCURRENT (all at once) or SEQUENTIAL (one at a time).
s1 every setting	:: How an iris crosses its opening: sweep (rings, from the rim in), spiral (a wedge turning outwards), rows (top and bottom in), columns (both sides in), or instant. Only the picture moves; the blocks are placed in one go whichever it is.
s1 every setting	:: How close a player must be, in blocks, for a mirror's banner to give way to the room it shows, and how near they must stay for it to stay on.
s1 every setting	:: How far below its plane a ceiling ring will look for the floor, in blocks. Its rings stack up from there, so it needs a floor near enough to reach.
s1 every setting	:: How far past its opening a mirror's room, or an open gate's far side, is drawn, N to N; past it this world shows through. N is ten chunks, about as far as a server sends. A gate shows the first N at once and fills in the rest behind. Lower it for a smoother view.
s1 every setting	:: How fast the beam gathers, rises, descends and fades: N is twice as fast, N half as fast. Read from N to N.
s1 every setting	:: How fast the rings run their countdown, rise, flash, return and refusal outline: N is twice as fast, N half as fast. Read from N to N; the countdown never drops under thirty ticks, so stepping clear stays possible.
s1 every setting	:: How loud beam sounds are. Volume also sets audible range: N is heard about sixteen blocks away.
s1 every setting	:: How loud gate sounds are. Volume also sets audible range: N carries about twenty-four blocks.
s1 every setting	:: How loud ring sounds are. Volume also sets audible range: N is heard about sixteen blocks away.
s1 every setting	:: How many gates one player may own. Building one more is refused, before any fare. A player with wormhole.gates.max.<n> has the highest such n instead, and wormhole.gates.unlimited lifts the limit; operators have that by default. N for no limit.
s1 every setting	:: How many mirrors one world may hold. N by default: a mirror is the door into its world, and a right-click scrolls through the mirrors of every other. N for no limit.
s1 every setting	:: How many ring pairs one player may own. N for no limit.
s1 every setting	:: How much the plugin logs: SEVERE, WARNING, INFO, CONFIG, FINE, FINER or FINEST, least to most.
s1 every setting	:: If set to true, a gate cannot dial a gate in another world, and nothing -- a player, a cart, a mob, an item or an arrow -- crosses between worlds by gate.
s1 every setting	:: If true, gates ignore permission nodes even when a Vault permission provider is installed: anyone may use, dial and travel by gate; only operators may build one; and removing, configuring or going to one with /wormhole go is left to operators and its owner.
s1 every setting	:: LOG_LEVEL = INFO
s1 every setting	:: Least distance in blocks between two gates in one world, centre to centre. Building, completing or placing a gate closer is refused, before any fare, unless the builder has wormhole.build.mindistance.bypass, which operators have by default. N for no limit.
s1 every setting	:: Log the blocks that building and taking down gates and rings place and remove to CoreProtect, so they can be rolled back. Requires CoreProtect. A running gate's water, levers and iris are not logged.
s1 every setting	:: Longest a wormhole may stay open, in seconds, however often it is re-dialled. Measured from when it first opened, so a gate re-triggered on a schedule cannot hold it open forever. N for no limit.
s1 every setting	:: MAP_SHOW_BEAMS = true
s1 every setting	:: MAP_SHOW_GATES = true
s1 every setting	:: MAP_SHOW_IRIS_GATES = true
s1 every setting	:: MAP_SHOW_MIRRORS = true
s1 every setting	:: MAP_SHOW_RINGS = true
s1 every setting	:: MAX_GATES_PER_PLAYER = N
s1 every setting	:: MAX_OPEN_SECONDS = N
s1 every setting	:: METRICS_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: MIN_GATE_DISTANCE = N
s1 every setting	:: MIRROR_APPROACH_MESSAGE = true
s1 every setting	:: MIRROR_ENTITY_LOAD_RADIUS = N
s1 every setting	:: MIRROR_PER_WORLD_LIMIT = N
s1 every setting	:: MIRROR_PROXIMITY_DISTANCE = N
s1 every setting	:: MIRROR_SHOW_ENTITIES = false
s1 every setting	:: MIRROR_SHOW_PLAYERS = false
s1 every setting	:: Minutes a gate preview, stood up by /wormhole gate build, stays up after its owner last used a gate build or gate preview command. At least N.
s1 every setting	:: Most blocks all build previews on the server may show at once, each one an entity its owner alone sees. Every shipped shape shown once is about ID. N turns previews off.
s1 every setting	:: Ops to Lab (ID) — world, PUBLIC, CONCURRENT/CONCURRENT
s1 every setting	:: PERMISSIONS_SUPPORT_DISABLE = false
s1 every setting	:: PETS_FOLLOW_OWNER = true
s1 every setting	:: PLACEHOLDERS_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: PLNXMAP_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: Played as a gate begins to dial.
s1 every setting	:: Played as a wormhole closes.
s1 every setting	:: Played at both ends as the pad closes.
s1 every setting	:: Played at both ends as the pad opens and the countdown starts.
s1 every setting	:: Played at both ends at the moment of transport.
s1 every setting	:: Played once as the wormhole establishes: the heavy splash, pitched down for size.
s1 every setting	:: Played once per chevron as it locks, pitch climbing through the sequence.
s1 every setting	:: Played once per ring as it leaves the pad and again as it returns, pitch climbing going out and falling coming back.
s1 every setting	:: Played once the column finishes descending at the destination.
s1 every setting	:: Played the instant a beam sequence starts.
s1 every setting	:: Played the instant the real teleport fires, partway through the rise.
s1 every setting	:: Played to a player a ring turns away, wherever they are standing. Heard by them alone.
s1 every setting	:: Played with the last chevron as it locks, before the wormhole forms.
s1 every setting	:: REDSTONE_EXTEND_OPEN_TIME = true
s1 every setting	:: RING_ANIMATION_SPEED = N
s1 every setting	:: RING_COOLDOWN_TICKS = N
s1 every setting	:: RING_DEFAULT_ACCESS = PRIVATE
