s1 every setting	:: RING_DEFAULT_LIGHT = REDSTONE_LAMP
s1 every setting	:: RING_DEFAULT_STYLE = CONCURRENT
s1 every setting	:: RING_MAX_CEILING_DROP = N
s1 every setting	:: RING_MAX_LINK_DISTANCE = N
s1 every setting	:: RING_MAX_PAIRS_PER_PLAYER = N
s1 every setting	:: RING_MIN_SEPARATION = N
s1 every setting	:: RING_OUTLINE_ON_REFUSAL = true
s1 every setting	:: RING_REACH = N
s1 every setting	:: RING_SOUNDS_ENABLED = true
s1 every setting	:: RING_SOUND_CLOSE = block.beacon.deactivate
s1 every setting	:: RING_SOUND_FLASH = block.beacon.power_select
s1 every setting	:: RING_SOUND_OPEN = block.beacon.activate
s1 every setting	:: RING_SOUND_REFUSED = block.note_block.bass
s1 every setting	:: RING_SOUND_RING = block.piston.extend
s1 every setting	:: RING_SOUND_VOLUME = N
s1 every setting	:: Range, Relay, Standard
s1 every setting	:: Register the %wormhole_...% PlaceholderAPI expansion. Requires PlaceholderAPI. Exposes gates_total, gates_open, gates_owned and nearest_gate.
s1 every setting	:: Relay has been closed, darkened and its iris opened.
s1 every setting	:: Required distance between ring anchors, in blocks. Overlap is refused regardless of this.
s1 every setting	:: SAME_WORLD_ONLY = false
s1 every setting	:: SERVER_LANGUAGE = en
s1 every setting	:: SHOW_GATE_WELCOME_MESSAGE = false
s1 every setting	:: SIGN_COLOR_GATE_NAME = DARK_AQUA
s1 every setting	:: SIGN_COLOR_NEIGHBOUR = GRAY
s1 every setting	:: SIGN_COLOR_NETWORK = GRAY
s1 every setting	:: SIGN_COLOR_OWNER = GRAY
s1 every setting	:: SIGN_COLOR_SELECTED = DARK_GREEN
s1 every setting	:: SIGN_DIAL_MATCH_MATERIAL = true
s1 every setting	:: SIGN_GLOWING_TEXT = false
s1 every setting	:: SQUAREMAP_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: Seconds a dialled gate stays open before shutting down. N keeps it open until something goes through.
s1 every setting	:: Seconds a gate stays activated, waiting to be dialled, before it times out.
s1 every setting	:: Seconds a player must wait between beams, when the cooldown above is enabled.
s1 every setting	:: Seconds a player must wait between gate trips, when the cooldown above is enabled.
s1 every setting	:: Send anonymous usage counts to bstats.org: Minecraft version, server software, and how many gates, rings, beams and mirrors are in use. No names, coordinates or addresses; bStats keeps a random id so it counts each server once. Set false to stop; bStats/config.yml turns it off for every plugin.
s1 every setting	:: Show gates, rings, public beam destinations and quantum mirrors on a BlueMap web map, each as its own marker set, with a line between dialled gates. Requires BlueMap. Players' private beam places are never shown.
s1 every setting	:: Show gates, rings, public beam destinations and quantum mirrors on a Dynmap web map, each as its own layer, with a line between dialled gates. Requires Dynmap. Players' private beam places are never shown.
s1 every setting	:: Show gates, rings, public beam destinations and quantum mirrors on a PlNxMap web map, each as its own layer, with a line between dialled gates. Requires PlNxMap, built for the server's Minecraft version. Players' private beam places are never shown.
s1 every setting	:: Show gates, rings, public beam destinations and quantum mirrors on a squaremap web map, each as its own layer, with a line between dialled gates. Requires squaremap, which runs on Paper. Players' private beam places are never shown.
s1 every setting	:: TIMEOUT_ACTIVATE = N
s1 every setting	:: TIMEOUT_SHUTDOWN = N
s1 every setting	:: The iris closing over a gate, pitched down a little since it is a shield rather than a door.
s1 every setting	:: The iris opening.
s1 every setting	:: The language of messages sent to the console and command blocks, such as de or pt_br (and, later, the log and text the server puts in the world); players see their own client's language. A message it lacks is in English. Only some messages are translatable so far; sign text stays English.
s1 every setting	:: The longest that tunnel may be, N to N blocks. It is a block longer for each block narrower the far gate is, and one more for the layer behind the opening that is its own size: four from Large to Standard, thirteen from Massive to Standard, sixteen from Grand to Minimal.
s1 every setting	:: The shortest that tunnel is, up to gate-view-funnel-length; none while gate-view-funnel is false. Above N, a gate the same size or bigger is seen down a straight tunnel too, and every tunnel runs straight for this or three fifths of this gate's opening, the longer, before it narrows. N for none.
s1 every setting	:: The soft running water an open wormhole makes while it stands there.
s1 every setting	:: Ticks a ring pair refuses to fire again after a cycle. Shared by both ends.
s1 every setting	:: UPDATE_CHECK = true
s1 every setting	:: USE_COOLDOWN_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: USE_COOLDOWN_SECONDS = N
s1 every setting	:: VIEW_DEPTH = N
s1 every setting	:: WORLDGUARD_ENABLED = false
s1 every setting	:: WORMHOLE_USE_IS_TELEPORT = false
s1 every setting	:: What a newly built ring pair starts as: PUBLIC or PRIVATE.
s1 every setting	:: What a ring turns to as the transport light passes through it. Set it apart from the pad light to make the transport its own moment.
s1 every setting	:: What an open gate shows once its kawoosh settles: horizon (the event horizon, as always), behind (where it goes, seen through the horizon), or open (where it goes, with no horizon). Upright gates with a frame round their opening, so not Minimal. An experiment, see #N.
s1 every setting	:: What the ring pad lights up as while it is working.
s1 every setting	:: When a gate dials a smaller one, gate-view shows the far side at the end of a tunnel the small gate's size, walled in this gate's portal material, so the view does not show past the small gate's walls and ceiling. False shows the whole view, as a gate the same size would.
s1 every setting	:: When a gate shape uses a frame material no material group claims, add that palette to gate-material-groups automatically. Ambiguous palettes are skipped. Set false to curate the list by hand.
s1 every setting	:: Whether a command the plugin names in chat can be clicked to run it, with hover text saying what it does. False sends plain text, as servers without Paper or Spigot do anyway.
s1 every setting	:: Whether a mirror names itself and the world it opens onto above the hotbar, while a player looks at it from within about six blocks. Only mirrors that go somewhere say anything.
s1 every setting	:: Whether a player arriving through a gate is told in chat which gate they arrived at. Gates only: rings and beams name their destination whatever this is set to.
s1 every setting	:: Whether a player-placed dial sign is converted to the gate's own sign material, keeping its text and facing. False leaves the sign exactly as placed.
s1 every setting	:: Whether a redstone signal on an already-open gate pushes its shutdown back. Never past max-open-seconds, so traffic can hold a gate open but not indefinitely.
s1 every setting	:: Whether an open gate's event horizon ripples, in rings out from its middle: as something goes in or comes out, and now and then while somebody is near. Upright gates only; the gate guide says which show it and how. Off while it is new.
s1 every setting	:: Whether beam travel has a per-player cooldown at all.
s1 every setting	:: Whether beaming makes any noise. Everything below is ignored when this is false.
s1 every setting	:: Whether gates with an iris code appear on the web map. Set false on a PvP server where a gate's location is a secret.
s1 every setting	:: Whether gates, and the lines between dialled gates, appear on the web map, as their own layer.
s1 every setting	:: Whether public beam destinations appear on the web map, as their own layer.
s1 every setting	:: Whether quantum mirrors appear on the web map, as their own layer.
s1 every setting	:: Whether rings make any noise. Everything below is ignored when this is false.
s1 every setting	:: Whether stargates make any noise. Everything below is ignored when this is false.
s1 every setting	:: Whether tamed wolves, cats and parrots that are following a player, not sitting, travel with them through gates, rings, beams and mirrors.
s1 every setting	:: Whether the creatures standing in a mirror's or an open gate's far room show through it, as stand-ins only the viewer sees. mirror-entity-load-radius keeps the far side loaded while watched; players only with mirror-show-players. The stand-ins are real entities, which other plugins count.
s1 every setting	:: Whether the plugin's own sign text glows. Off, because glow outlines every character and fights the colours below; true is more legible from a distance.
s1 every setting	:: Whether transport rings appear on the web map, as their own layer.
s1 every setting	:: Whether wormhole.use is needed to travel at all. False lets anyone travel but only permitted players activate a gate; true limits travel too.
s1 every setting	:: With mirror-show-entities on too, whether the players in a view's far room show as well: a mannequin from N.N, an armour stand wearing their head before. Off by default: it shows who is at the destination, by their real skin, not a disguise's. Never anyone hidden by hidePlayer; a hide done in packets is not seen.
s1 every setting	:: With mirror-show-entities on, how many chunks in front of a watched view's far side are held, as /forceload holds them, so its creatures show at once: N at N, about N loaded with the ring round them, which can generate terrain. N holds nothing. Read up to N.
s1 every setting	:: error :: You have no half-built ring pair.
s1 every setting	:: error :: You lack the permissions to do this.
